TOTEM HAKA (25s · 2D Hand-Drawn Cartoon · 30fps)

Tone: Intense haka energy + comedic exaggeration
Look: Flat 2D paper-cutout animation, bold outlines, saturated colors, smear-frames, ink FX
Punchline: “When your ancestors perform a haka just to intimidate Monday.”

🖼️ STYLE & LOOK (Global)

Pure 2D hand-drawn animation, flat surfaces, no shading or gradients.
Rough textured paper background; characters look like cut-out illustrations brought to life.
Thick black outlines, saturated fill colors, geometric exaggeration.
Smear-frame effects for fast arm/leg motions.
Ink splatters, glyph bursts, and rippling lines used as FX.
Camera is locked in a 2D plane: pans, zooms, snap-ins — no 3D rotation.

🔧 GLOBAL MOTION RULES

No still frames: totem performs subtle micro-motions even during pauses.
Birds and spiders always react — shaking, hopping, flinching — for comedic timing.
Stomps produce screen shakes and paper ripple distortions.
Ink shockwaves radiate outward during intense haka shouts.
Smear frames appear automatically in fast arm swings and jumps.
Sound-choreography: visuals sync to stomps, chants, and chest beats.
🔊 AUDIO DESIGN (Guiding Notes)
Deep, rhythmic percussive stomps (cardboard thuds).
Haka-style grunts and breaths (nonsense syllables to avoid cultural misuse).
Ink splatter “pwip” sounds.
Birds chirping as hype crew.
Final shout with reverberating ink shockwave.

🕒 SCENE-BY-SCENE BREAKDOWN (25 seconds)
0.0–1.5s — SCENE 1: Totem Awakens

Close-up of the static totem on paper.
Sudden twitching.
Eyes snap open with shutter-like flaps.
Birds hop upward in fright.
Low grunt: “Hoh!”
Tiny ink freckles vibrate.

1.5–3.5s — SCENE 2: Rise Into Stance

Zoom out as the totem pops off the page like a cardboard cutout.
It lands with a heavy THUMP, shaking the frame.
Arms snap outward into wide haka stance.
Spiders scuttle around to watch like spectators.

3.5–6.0s — SCENE 3: Chest-Beat Warmup

Medium shot.
Totem beats its chest rapidly: TAK-TAK-TAK-TAK!
Ink splashes burst with each hit.
Birds nod aggressively with hype-crew energy.

6.0–8.0s — SCENE 4: Face of Fury

Totem leans into the camera.
Eyes widen, eyebrows flare, tongue stretches down past chin.
Colors invert briefly in a dramatic intimidation flash.
Deep growl: “Rrah!”

8.0–10.5s — SCENE 5: Foot-Stomp Pattern

Wide shot.
LEFT stomp → screen shakes.
RIGHT stomp → screen shakes harder.
LEFT stomp → ink radiates.
BOTH FEET SLAM → paper background ripples like water.
Spiders bounce helplessly in rhythm.

10.5–12.5s — SCENE 6: Rapid Arm Swings

Totem performs lightning-fast geometric arm slashes.
Smear frames stretch arms into zig-zag triangles.
Birds scatter, then return like cheerleaders doing tiny kicks.

12.5–14.5s — SCENE 7: Chant of Power

Totem lifts chin in ritual posture.
Calls out rhythmic haka-like nonsense syllables:
“KA! MA! TE! KA! MA! TE!”
Dark ink rings pulse outward in concentric energy waves.

14.5–17.5s — SCENE 8: Ancestor Split-Forms

Totem splits into three translucent duplicates:
Center = red
Left = yellow
Right = purple
All perform synchronized haka motions with echoing choral grunts.
Birds freeze, awe-struck.
Paper background vibrates with layered patterns.

17.5–20.0s — SCENE 9: Power Build

The three duplicates merge back with a dramatic WHOOMP.
Totem slams both fists on the ground, creating a swirling vortex of ink glyphs.
Chants deepen, drums intensify.

20.0–23.0s — SCENE 10: Final Haka Challenge

Totem jumps forward aggressively (still flat 2D).
Extreme close-up: eyes huge, tongue out, face fierce.
It unleashes ultimate roar:
“HAAAAAHH!”
Massive ink shockwave blasts outward, flattening spiders and sending birds tumbling offscreen.

23.0–25.0s — SCENE 11: Comedy Cool-Down

Totem freezes. Blinks.
Suddenly becomes shy, posture normal.
Waves awkwardly to camera like: “Sorry… got carried away.”
Birds crawl back in, judging it.
One spider raises a tiny sign: 10/10.